# Written by scripts/gen_build_info.py at build time and baked into the image:
# the branch, the build number and the commit. Never committed, because a copy
# in the history would be one build permanently out of date. The changelog
# itself is NOT here - it is written by hand in backend/app/changelog.py.
backend/app/build_info.json

# Round change-documents are a DELIVERY MECHANISM, not source. apply_docx.py
# stages with `git add -A`, so without this every round pushes its own .docx
# into the repo and the history fills up with binaries nobody reads from git.
# Already pushed some? `git rm -r --cached "*.docx"` then commit — that untracks
# them without deleting the files on disk.
*.docx
~$*.docx
# ...except documentation written to be shared, which lives under docs/.
!docs/*.docx

# Local agent/editor configuration. Machine-specific paths, no value to anyone
# cloning this.
.claude/

# Security review material. Written against ONE deployment -- its topology, its
# compensating controls, its open questions. Useful to the team that owns that
# deployment and to nobody else, so it stays out of a public repository.
docs/RED_TEAM_BRIEF.md
docs/PENTEST_CHECKLIST_HE.docx
